{"timestamp":1774907387097,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"c5227999-a355-4987-9776-feb331ae5c82","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01X6USyQUYm3csa4ksprkzUz","payload":{"session_id":"c5227999-a355-4987-9776-feb331ae5c82","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-3b78e2c1/c5227999-a355-4987-9776-feb331ae5c82.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/3b78e2c1","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/3b78e2c1/.pinata/specs/issue-11-adw-3b78e2c1-sdlc_planner-prevent-duplicate-clone-title.md","content":"# Plan: Prevent duplicate Fragment Title for cloned cards in M@S Studio\n\n## Summary\nWhen a user clones a card in M@S Studio, the clone dialog pre-populates the title with the original fragment's title but does not check for uniqueness. This adds a `generateUniqueTitle` helper to `utils.js` that appends a numeric suffix (`-1`, `-2`, \u2026) when a title collision is detected within the same folder path, and wires it into the `copyFragment` flow in `mas-repository.js`. Both `editor-panel.js` and `mas-fragment-editor.js` are updated so `titleClone` is pre-populated on dialog open, ensuring the dedup runs even when the user accepts the default title unchanged.\n\n## Task Description\n- Add a pure `generateUniqueTitle(baseTitle, existingTitles)` helper to `studio/src/utils.js`.\n- Pre-populate `this.titleClone` with the current fragment's title in `showClone()` (both `editor-panel.js` and `mas-fragment-editor.js`).\n- In `mas-repository.js#copyFragment`, resolve the effective clone title (from user input or fragment title), collect existing titles from `Store.fragments.list.data` scoped to the same folder path, call `generateUniqueTitle`, and pass the deduplicated title when saving the cloned fragment.\n- Add unit tests for `generateUniqueTitle` in `studio/test/utils.test.js`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Role |\n|------|------|\n| `studio/src/utils.js` | Add `generateUniqueTitle` helper |\n| `studio/src/mas-repository.js` | Call dedup in `copyFragment` (line 1012) |\n| `studio/src/editor-panel.js` | Pre-populate `titleClone` in `showClone()` (line 620) |\n| `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` | Pre-populate `titleClone` in `showClone()` (line 1088) |\n| `studio/test/utils.test.js` | Unit tests for new helper |\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Add `generateUniqueTitle` to `studio/src/utils.js`\n- Export a new function `generateUniqueTitle(baseTitle, existingTitles)` where `existingTitles` is a `Set` or array of title strings already in the scope.\n- Strip any existing trailing `-N` numeric suffix from `baseTitle` to get the stem (e.g. `lucy-card-1` \u2192 `lucy-card`).\n- If the base title is not in `existingTitles`, return it unchanged.\n- Otherwise, increment from 1 upward (`${stem}-1`, `${stem}-2`, \u2026) until a title not in `existingTitles` is found, then return it.\n- Regex for trailing suffix detection: `/^(.*)-(\\d+)$/`.\n\n### 2. Pre-populate `titleClone` on dialog open \u2014 `editor-panel.js`\n- In `showClone()` (line 620), after setting `this.showCloneDialog = true`, add:\n  ```js\n  this.titleClone = this.fragment?.title ?? '';\n  ```\n- This ensures `titleClone` is set even if the user accepts the default without typing.\n\n### 3. Pre-populate `titleClone` on dialog open \u2014 `mas-fragment-editor.js`\n- In `showClone()` (line 1088), after setting `this.showCloneDialog = true`, add:\n  ```js\n  this.titleClone = this.fragment?.title ?? '';\n  ```\n\n### 4. Deduplicate clone title in `mas-repository.js#copyFragment`\n- At the top of `copyFragment` (line 1012), before calling `aem.sites.cf.fragments.copy`:\n  1. Determine the effective title: `const effectiveTitle = updatedTitle || this.fragmentInEdit.title;`\n  2. Derive the folder path from `this.fragmentInEdit.path` by stripping the last segment: `const folderPath = this.fragmentInEdit.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/');`\n  3. Collect titles of all loaded fragments in the same folder from `Store.fragments.list.data`:\n     ```js\n     const existingTitles = Store.fragments.list.data.get()\n         .map(s => s.get?.()?.path?.startsWith(folderPath) ? s.get()?.title : null)\n         .filter(Boolean);\n     ```\n  4. Call `const uniqueTitle = generateUniqueTitle(effectiveTitle, existingTitles);` (import from `./utils.js`).\n  5. Pass `uniqueTitle` as `updatedTitle` throughout the rest of the method. Replace the existing `needsSave` check so that `uniqueTitle` (never falsy \u2014 at minimum equal to `effectiveTitle`) drives the title update:\n     ```js\n     const needsSave = uniqueTitle !== result.title || osi;\n     if (needsSave) {\n         result.title = uniqueTitle;\n         // \u2026 existing osi field update \u2026\n     }\n     ```\n- Add `import { generateUniqueTitle, showToast } from './utils.js';` if `generateUniqueTitle` is not already imported (merge into existing import).\n\n### 5. Add unit tests in `studio/test/utils.test.js`\n- Test `generateUniqueTitle` with:\n  - No collision \u2192 returns base title unchanged.\n  - Collision with base title \u2192 returns `baseTitle-1`.\n  - Collision with `baseTitle` and `baseTitle-1` \u2192 returns `baseTitle-2`.\n  - Input already has a `-N` suffix and there is a collision \u2192 strips and re-increments correctly.\n  - Empty `existingTitles` \u2192 always returns base title.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Cloning a fragment whose title already exists in the same folder produces a clone titled `{original}-1`.\n- Cloning again when `{original}-1` exists produces `{original}-2`.\n- Cloning when no title collision exists leaves the title unchanged.\n- The original fragment's title is never modified.\n- Manual edits to the title field in the clone dialog are respected and still deduplicated.\n- `generateUniqueTitle` is a pure function with no side effects, fully covered by unit tests.\n- `node --check studio/src/utils.js` and `node --check studio/src/mas-repository.js` both pass.\n\n## Validation Commands\n- `node --check studio/src/utils.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/mas-repository.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/editor-panel.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X6USyQUYm3csa4ksprkzUz"}}
